---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import { site, supportMailto } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Cook Club Privacy Policy, including data collected, providers, retention, deletion, and contact information."
>
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    intro="This Privacy Policy explains how Cook Club collects, uses, stores, and deletes information for the Cook Club app and website."
  >
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {site.lastUpdated}</p>
    <p>
      Cook Club is the app brand for this service and is developed by
      {site.developer}. For privacy questions, contact
      <a href={supportMailto}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Cook Club may collect the following information when you use the app:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Account details such as name, email address, user ID, username, profile details, and profile image.</li>
      <li>Authentication information from Apple or Google when you choose those sign-in methods, such as the account identifier and profile information they share with Cook Club.</li>
      <li>User content such as recipes, recipe images, review text and images, comments, collections, follows, meal plans, and shopping lists.</li>
      <li>Subscription status, entitlement information, and related purchase identifiers from Apple, Google, and Adapty. Cook Club does not receive your full payment card details.</li>
      <li>Legal acceptance records, including the Terms version and acceptance time.</li>
      <li>Safety records including user blocks, reports, report evidence snapshots, moderation decisions, and audit history.</li>
      <li>Device push tokens used to send notifications you enable.</li>
      <li>Diagnostics, crash and performance data, server logs, request metadata, and app or device information used to operate, secure, debug, and improve Cook Club. Default user-identifying information is not sent with Sentry diagnostics.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accounts, authentication, recipe storage, meal planning, shopping lists, social features, comments, reviews, and notifications.</li>
      <li>Process recipe imports, AI-assisted recipe features, and image uploads.</li>
      <li>Manage subscriptions and access to paid features.</li>
      <li>Respond to support, privacy, safety, moderation, and account deletion requests.</li>
      <li>Protect Cook Club from abuse, spam, security incidents, and policy violations.</li>
      <li>Maintain and improve reliability, performance, and user experience.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service Providers and Processors</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club uses third-party providers to run the service. These providers
      process information only as needed to provide their services to Cook Club.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Cloudflare for hosting, Workers, routing, logs, and image/object storage.</li>
      <li>Neon/Postgres for database hosting.</li>
      <li>Expo for app services, push notifications, and app delivery tooling.</li>
      <li>Apple and Google for authentication, app distribution, and subscription platform services.</li>
      <li>Adapty for subscription status and entitlement management.</li>
      <li>Sentry for crash and performance diagnostics.</li>
      <li>Resend for transactional email such as verification and support-related email.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club does not sell your personal information. Some profile, recipe,
      review, image, comment, follow, and activity information may be visible to
      other Cook Club users when you use social or shared features. We may also
      disclose information when required by law, to protect rights and safety, or
      to investigate abuse or security incidents.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club uses encryption in transit for public app and website traffic.
      Access to production systems is limited to the people and services that
      need it to operate Cook Club. No online service can guarantee absolute
      security, but Cook Club is designed to reduce unnecessary data exposure.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club keeps account information and user content while your account is
      active or as needed to provide the service. You can delete your account in
      the app from <strong>Settings &gt; Delete Account</strong>, or request deletion
      by emailing <a href={supportMailto}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      After account deletion, Cook Club deletes or de-identifies account data and
      user content unless retention is required for legal, security, fraud
      prevention, dispute, backup, tax, accounting, or payment/subscription
      record reasons. Deleting your Cook Club account does not cancel Apple or
      Google subscriptions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reports and their immutable evidence snapshots may be retained after the
      source content is hidden or deleted so Cook Club can investigate abuse,
      enforce its rules, prevent repeat harm, and maintain an audit trail. When
      an account is deleted, reporter identity is deleted or de-identified
      unless a limited retention exception above applies. Block records are
      deleted with the blocking account.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club is not directed to children under 13. If you believe a child has
      provided personal information to Cook Club, contact us so we can review
      and delete it where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Cook Club may update this Privacy Policy as the app changes. The latest
      version will always be available at <a href="/privacy">cookclub.app/privacy</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
